<h1>RageBaiting — Master Prompts & Complete Specification Document</h1>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Document Summary:</strong> This document contains the complete collection of prompts, architectural specifications, design constraints, and reverse-psychology logic used to design, build, and refine the <strong>RageBaiting</strong> interactive website.
</div>

<hr/>

<h2>1. Overview of the Application</h2>
<p><strong>RageBaiting</strong> is a responsive, funny digital endurance experience built using pure vanilla HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript. It incorporates reverse psychology, humorous micro-interactions, fake operating system controls, and synthesizer-driven audio feedback to entertain users through deliberate digital frustration.</p>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Core Milestone</th>
    <th>Mechanism</th>
    <th>User Psychological Impact</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Rage Vehicle Admission</strong></td>
    <td>3 Mandatory simulated login attempts with 1% &rarr; 99% throttle and a 4-second engine freeze.</td>
    <td>Builds anticipation before intentionally failing twice and rewarding persistence.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Achievement Modal</strong></td>
    <td>Triple Auth Survivor diploma conferred upon completing the 3rd attempt.</td>
    <td>Validates the ridiculousness of logging in 3 times for a basic website.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Reverse Popups (1-55)</strong></td>
    <td>Only "KEEP POPUP" and "CLOSE POPUP" buttons. Reverse psychology: clicking Keep closes it; clicking Close refuses to close.</td>
    <td>Pure comedic subversion of typical UI conventions.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Graduation & Inverter</strong></td>
    <td>Half-screen dual graduation quotes with full-screen color and reality inversion mode.</td>
    <td>Satirizes user accomplishments and flips normal meanings into harsh comedic truths.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Fake Laptop Controls</strong></td>
    <td>In-browser desktop window with Minimize ("Can't minimize problems"), Maximize (shrinks tiny), and Close ("Premium feature").</td>
    <td>Subverts expected operating system control behavior.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>250 Years Diagnostic</strong></td>
    <td>Quantum lifetime calculation citing 250 years wasted and 0.0001% productivity.</td>
    <td>Highlights the deliberate pointlessness of digital time-wasting.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Boss Surveillance Exit</strong></td>
    <td>"Wait! Is your boss behind you?!" with reverse exit logic and the "I will grab you again" hook.</td>
    <td>Workplace parody that traps the user if they try to leave, and exits if they ask to stay.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>2. Prompt 1 — Original Full Specification Prompt</h2>
<p>Below is the complete, unabridged original prompt provided for the foundation of the project:</p>

<div class="prompt-box">
# Build RageBaiting — Complete Working Website

Build a complete, responsive, funny ragebait website called RageBaiting using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

Prioritize working functionality, a polished interface, and a complete user flow. Keep the project simple with three main files:
- index.html
- style.css
- script.js

Do not use React, complex frameworks, backend servers, or paid APIs. The website must work by opening index.html in a browser.

## 1. Login Page — Three Login Attempts
Create a modern, attractive login page with:
- Username field
- Password field
- Login button
- Dark modern background
- Funny RageBaiting branding
- Responsive layout

### Login functionality
1. The user enters their username and password.
2. Clicking Login starts a loading animation.
3. Display a progress bar that quickly moves from 1% to 99%.
4. At 99%, pause for 4 seconds.
5. Show this error: "Shit! Something went wrong. Please log in again."
6. Return to the login page and require another login attempt.
7. Repeat until the user submits the login form three times.

After the third login, show an achievement popup:
"CONGRATULATIONS! 🎉"
"You logged in THREE TIMES just to open this basic website."
"Your productivity has officially left the chat."
Add a working Continue button.

## 2. Welcome Popup Ragebait — 55 Popups
After the third login, show a welcome popup repeatedly, one after another, until 55 popups have appeared.

### Popup content
"WELCOME, USER! 🎊"
"We are very happy that you logged in. Again."
Display a counter: "Welcome Popup: 17/55"
The number must update correctly for every popup.

### Continuous popup behavior
- Automatically display the next popup after the current popup is dismissed.
- Do not display all 55 popups simultaneously.
- Keep the same popup design but change the counter.
- Add a short animation whenever the next popup appears.
- Play a short "ting ting" sound when each popup appears.
- Include a working mute/unmute button.
- Sound should work after the user's first interaction with the website.

### Popup buttons
- KEEP IT 😊: Close current popup, show next popup. After 55, open profile page.
- CLOSE IT ❌: Confirmation: "Are you sure you want to close happiness?"
- SKIP 55 POPUPS ⏭️: Stop popup sequence immediately and proceed directly to profile.

## 3. Profile Page and Fake Laptop Controls
Include:
- Username entered on the login page
- Profile avatar & Welcome message
- Fake laptop application window
- Website lifetime calculator
- Rage Level indicator & Restart button

Three fake laptop controls at top-right:
- Minimize: "You wanted to minimize your problems?" (keep window visible).
- Maximize: Shrink fake window to tiny size, display "Maximum disappointment achieved", provide restore button.
- Close: "Closing is a premium feature" (keep window open).

## 4. Website Lifetime Calculator — 250 Years
Title: "YOUR WEBSITE LIFE EXPECTANCY 🤡"
Large animated number: 250 YEARS
Subtitle: "Estimated lifetime on this website."
Additional text: "Even though you have done absolutely nothing here."
Report:
- Time spent doing nothing: 250 years
- Productivity: 0.0001%
- Login attempts: 3
- Your future plans: Cancelled
- Website commitment: Forever

## 5. Lifetime Section — Close Website Prank
Button: CLOSE THIS WEBSITE
Confirmation popup:
"OK, WE ARE GOING TO THE SOUTH SIDE! 🚶"
"You are not delivering us anywhere. You've been doing nothing on this website for 250 years!"
"Please reconsider your decision to leave. Your lifetime subscription has just begun."
Buttons:
- FINE, I'LL STAY 😭: Closes popup, shows "Another 250 years added to your account."
- I'M LEAVING ANYWAY: Shows "You escaped! Your 250-year sentence has been cancelled", provides working Restart button.
</div>

