<h2>3. Prompt 2 — The Opposite Function & Screen Inverter Prompt</h2>
<p>Below is the modification prompt refining the popup interactions, reversing the button functionality, adding the Rage Vehicle concept, and introducing the half-screen graduating statements with the reality inverter:</p>

<div class="prompt-box">
im I'm not satisfied this website at all I thought it should be In this website when we logged in it will be showing skip the proper etcetera close it keep it the proper so this keep the proper option removing and only keep the corruption keep the proper and close the property but the function is like if we click on the pop up then it closes the pop up if we click on the close the pop up then it will keep that pop make opposite function then after that when we log in with some Again which is rage vehicle to new users and add some graduating statements which will with some inverters which will show at half this in the whole website and make it simple different
 and make it simple different
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Decoded Key Requirements:</strong>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Remove Skip Button:</strong> Eliminate the skip button entirely from the popup sequence.</li>
    <li><strong>Opposite Logic:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Clicking <code>KEEP POPUP 😊</code> (or clicking the popup card) &rarr; <strong>Actually CLOSES the popup and advances</strong>.</li>
        <li>Clicking <code>CLOSE POPUP ❌</code> &rarr; <strong>Refuses to close, shakes furiously, and KEEPS IT</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Rage Vehicle Theme:</strong> Transform login attempts into 3 laps of a vehicle driver's test where the engine reaches 99 MPH and stalls for 4 seconds.</li>
    <li><strong>Graduating Statements & Screen Inverter:</strong> Half-screen top banner showing normal statements vs inverted realities, accompanied by an interactive screen inverter toggle that flips the entire website's visual color spectrum.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<hr/>

<h2>4. Prompt 3 — Boss Surveillance Alert & Reverse Escape Prompt</h2>
<p>Below is the modification prompt regarding the workplace boss detection and the reverse exit mechanism:</p>

<div class="prompt-box">
When they'll ask when you click on the close this website then there are two option menu click on click close on the website it should not be sure it should you want to give us from a maybe your boss at this section with some ....ing but I will grab you again at this
 your boss at this section with some funny emoji and if we click on leave OK keep it me on this website then it will leave this website and saying you are leaving but I will grab you again at this your boss at this section with some funny emoji and if we click on leave OK keep it me on this website then it will leave this website and saying you are leaving but I will grab you again at this modificationadd ths on wbsiteei
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Decoded Key Requirements:</strong>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Boss Surveillance Theme:</strong> When clicking "CLOSE THIS WEBSITE", trigger a Code Red Boss Alert: <em>"WAIT! IS YOUR BOSS BEHIND YOU?! 👔👀"</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Reverse Exit Buttons:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li><code>OK, KEEP ME ON THIS WEBSITE 😭</code>: Clicking to stay actually <strong>leaves the website</strong> and launches the escape screen!</li>
        <li><code>I'M LEAVING ANYWAY 🏃‍♂️</code>: Clicking to leave is <strong>DENIED</strong> by your manager, adds +250 years of mandatory overtime, and keeps you trapped!</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>"I Will Grab You Again" Farewell:</strong> The escape screen explicitly warns:
      <br/><em>"YOU ARE LEAVING... BUT I WILL GRAB YOU AGAIN! 🪝😈👔"</em>
      <br/>With a working restart button to experience the trap again.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

