<h2>5. Technical Architecture Summary</h2>

<h3>5.1 State Machine Representation</h3>
<pre style="background:#1e293b; color:#f8fafc; padding:12pt; border-radius:6pt; font-family:'Consolas', monospace;">
const state = {
  loginAttempts: 0,       // 0 to 3 mandatory attempts
  maxLoginAttempts: 3,
  username: "SpeedRacer",
  isLoggingIn: false,
  popupIndex: 1,          // 1 to 55 counter
  maxPopups: 55,
  soundMuted: false,      // Audio toggle
  lifetimeYears: 250,     // Increments by +250 upon overtime
  isPopupActive: false,
  isInvertedMode: false,  // Inverter filter flag
  gradIndex: 0
};
</pre>

<h3>5.2 Audio Synthesis (No External Dependencies)</h3>
<p>All sound effects (dual-tone ting-ting chimes, error buzzers, inverter sweeps, and fanfares) are synthesized programmatically using the browser's built-in <strong>Web Audio API</strong> (<code>AudioContext</code>), ensuring zero 404 network errors or missing asset files.</p>

